"s1-threshold": {
"svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 440 130\" class=\"fig\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A one-number classifier: everything above T is predicted malignant. With T = 2.25 only one point is wrong (the benign 3.0). No single cut can be perfect, because a malignant 2.5 sits left of a benign 3.0.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah-s1t\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"ah\"/></marker><clipPath id=\"cp-s1t\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"440\" height=\"130\"/></clipPath></defs><line x1=\"34.8\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"405.2\" y2=\"60\" class=\"ax\"/><text x=\"53.8\" y=\"86\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><circle cx=\"53.8\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"d1\"><title>1.0 cm: benign</title></circle><text x=\"101.2\" y=\"86\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1.5</text><circle cx=\"101.2\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"d1\"><title>1.5 cm: benign</title></circle><text x=\"148.8\" y=\"86\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><circle cx=\"148.8\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"d1\"><title>2.0 cm: benign</title></circle><text x=\"196.2\" y=\"86\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2.5</text><rect x=\"190.2\" y=\"54\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"><title>2.5 cm: malignant</title></rect><text x=\"243.8\" y=\"86\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><circle cx=\"243.8\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"d1\"><title>3.0 cm: benign</title></circle><text x=\"291.2\" y=\"86\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3.5</text><rect x=\"285.2\" y=\"54\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"><title>3.5 cm: malignant</title></rect><text x=\"338.8\" y=\"86\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><rect x=\"332.8\" y=\"54\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"><title>4.0 cm: malignant</title></rect><text x=\"386.2\" y=\"86\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4.5</text><rect x=\"380.2\" y=\"54\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"><title>4.5 cm: malignant</title></rect><line x1=\"172.5\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"172.5\" y2=\"96\" class=\"guide2\"/><text x=\"172.5\" y=\"14\" class=\"tb\" text-anchor=\"middle\">threshold T = 2.25</text><text x=\"103.6\" y=\"110\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">← predict benign</text><text x=\"288.9\" y=\"110\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">predict malignant →</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"124\" r=\"4\" class=\"d1\"></circle><text x=\"48\" y=\"128\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"start\">benign</text><rect x=\"106\" y=\"120\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"></rect><text x=\"118\" y=\"128\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"start\">malignant</text><text x=\"405.2\" y=\"128\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"end\">tumour size (cm)</text></svg>",
"caption": "A one-number classifier: everything above T is predicted malignant. With T = 2.25 only one point is wrong (the benign 3.0). No single cut can be perfect, because a malignant 2.5 sits left of a benign 3.0."
},
