"s7-xor": {
"svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 440 210\" class=\"fig\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"XOR can't be split by any line in the original plane, but the single feature z = x₁x₂ puts both + points at z = 1 and both − points at z = −1. The boundary z = 0 maps back to the two coordinate axes.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah-s7x\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"ah\"/></marker><clipPath id=\"cp-s7x\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"440\" height=\"210\"/></clipPath></defs><rect x=\"20\" y=\"28\" width=\"160\" height=\"150\" rx=\"4\" class=\"panel\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"178\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"28\" class=\"gr\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"103\" x2=\"180\" y2=\"103\" class=\"gr\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"56.1\" r=\"5.5\" class=\"d1\"><title>+ (1, 1)</title></circle><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"149.9\" r=\"5.5\" class=\"d1\"><title>+ (-1, -1)</title></circle><rect x=\"144.5\" y=\"144.4\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"><title>− (1, -1)</title></rect><rect x=\"44.5\" y=\"50.6\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"><title>− (-1, 1)</title></rect><text x=\"100\" y=\"20\" class=\"tb\" text-anchor=\"middle\">XOR: no straight line works</text><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"240\" y2=\"100\" class=\"arr\" marker-end=\"url(#ah-s7x)\"/><text x=\"215\" y=\"90\" class=\"tb\" text-anchor=\"middle\">z = x₁x₂</text><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"420\" y2=\"100\" class=\"ax\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"118\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">-1</text><text x=\"390\" y=\"118\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"346\" y=\"118\" class=\"ts\" text-anchor=\"start\">0</text><rect x=\"284.5\" y=\"84.5\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"></rect><rect x=\"284.5\" y=\"70.5\" width=\"11\" height=\"11\" rx=\"1.5\" class=\"d2\"></rect><circle cx=\"390\" cy=\"90\" r=\"5.5\" class=\"d1\"></circle><circle cx=\"390\" cy=\"76\" r=\"5.5\" class=\"d1\"></circle><line x1=\"340\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"150\" class=\"l2\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"36\" class=\"tb\" text-anchor=\"middle\">z = 0 separates perfectly</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"170\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">back in (x₁, x₂): x₁x₂ = 0,</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"186\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">i.e. the two axes</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"196\" class=\"ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">same signs → +, different → −</text></svg>",
"caption": "XOR can't be split by any line in the original plane, but the single feature z = x₁x₂ puts both + points at z = 1 and both − points at z = −1. The boundary z = 0 maps back to the two coordinate axes."
},
